1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,940
If you want to drive in Japan as a tourist, check your driving documents before you travel.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:12,080
Many visitors need a booklet-type International Driving Permit from the 1949 Geneva Convention.

3
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:15,000
A card or phone version is not enough.

4
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:25,840
Some visitors from places such as Germany, France, Switzerland, Belgium, Monaco, and Taiwan use their own license with an official Japanese translation.

5
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:31,080
At the rental counter, staff may also check your passport and entry stamp.

6
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:36,180
Rules can change, so check official information before your trip.

7
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:40,840
Book the car early, especially in rural areas or during holidays.

8
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:47,320
At the counter, give your name, reservation number, passport, and driving documents.

9
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:52,220
Ask about insurance, the return time, and the fuel rule.

10
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:56,200
Many rental shops ask you to return the car with a full tank.

11
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:59,180
Before you leave, walk around the car with staff.

12
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:03,260
Check scratches and dents, and take photos if the company allows it.

13
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:06,660
In Japan, cars drive on the left side of the road.

14
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:09,360
The driver sits on the right side of the car.

15
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:13,480
Go slowly at first, because turns can feel different.

16
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:17,020
Everyone must wear a seat belt.

17
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:18,780
Do not use your phone while driving.

18
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:21,280
Do not drink alcohol before driving.

19
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:25,120
At railroad crossings, stop and check both ways.

20
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:27,880
On expressways, you pay tolls.

21
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:32,540
Ask if the car has ETC, a toll card system, or if you should pay in cash.

22
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:37,520
Parking can be difficult in busy cities, so look for a real parking lot.

23
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:41,360
Do not park on the street unless signs clearly allow it.

24
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:46,840
For navigation, ask for an English or foreign-language car navigation system.

25
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:53,680
In rural areas, English signs may be limited, so save your hotel address and rental shop address.

26
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:58,160
Before returning the car, refuel if the rule says full tank.

27
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:03,360
Keep the receipt, arrive before the return time, and ask staff to check the car.

28
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:06,920
Risa rents a car for a two-day trip in Yamanashi.

29
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:12,400
She asks the rental staff about documents, insurance, tolls, and returning the car.

30
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:13,280
Good morning.

31
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,180
Welcome to Sakura Rent-a-Car.

32
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:16,500
How can I help you?

33
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,380
Risa: Hi.

34
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:20,120
I have a reservation under Ogino.

35
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:21,220
Thank you.

36
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,600
May I see your passport and driving documents?

37
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:26,070
Risa: Sure.

38
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:29,360
Here is my passport and my International Driving Permit.

39
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:30,300
Thank you.

40
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,440
This permit is the booklet type.

41
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:33,840
It is valid for Japan.

42
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:35,930
Risa: Great.

43
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:37,760
What insurance is included?

44
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,040
Basic insurance is included.

45
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:42,240
You can add extra coverage for accidents.

46
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:45,400
Risa: I see.

47
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,760
Does this car have ETC for toll roads?

48
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,920
Yes, it has ETC.

49
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:52,300
You can rent an ETC card from us.

50
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:54,180
Risa: Good.

51
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:56,060
Should I return the car with a full tank?

52
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:59,740
Yes, please return it with a full tank and bring the receipt.

53
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:03,180
Risa: What time should I return it on Sunday?

54
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:05,660
Please return it by 6 p.m.

55
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:09,440
Risa: Before I leave, can we check the scratches together?

56
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:10,520
Of course.

57
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:12,440
Let's check the car together now.

58
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:14,740
Risa: Thank you.

59
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,600
I will drive slowly at first.

60
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:17,620
Good idea.

61
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:20,680
In Japan, please drive on the left.
